{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% from "macros.html.j2" import source_mark %}
{% block title %}Where I differ from the expert, {{ meta.target }}{% endblock %}
{% block heading %}Where I differ from the expert{% endblock %}
{% block main %}
<p class="lead">Grant Samuel published a range and no preferred value, so the bridge starts at the midpoint of its range. Each step swaps one group of inputs from the expert's value to mine, in the order shown, and each change is the effect of that swap with the steps before it already made. Where an explanation gives the expert's A$<span class="num" data-key="expert_business_operations_value_aud_m_low">{{ bridge.expert_operations_low }}</span>m to A$<span class="num" data-key="expert_business_operations_value_aud_m_high">{{ bridge.expert_operations_high }}</span>m, that is its value of business operations, before net debt. Where I kept the expert's input the step is zero, and the explanation says what I kept and, for the discount rate, the forecast and terminal growth, what a different value would give.</p>
{% include "gap_bridge_chart.html.j2" %}
<section aria-labelledby="steps-heading">
  <h2 id="steps-heading">Each step explained</h2>
  {% for step in bridge.steps %}
  <article id="step-{{ step.id }}" class="step">
    <h3>{{ step.label }}</h3>
    <p class="note">Change {{ step.change }}. Value after this step {{ step.after }}. Booklet pages: {{ step.sources }}.</p>
    <p>{{ step.explanation }}</p>
    {% if step.inputs %}
    <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Inputs changed in {{ step.label }}">
      <table class="figures">
        <caption>Inputs in this step</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Input</th><th scope="col">Unit</th><th scope="col" class="num">Expert</th><th scope="col" class="num">Mine</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for change in step.inputs %}
          <tr><th scope="row">{{ change.key }}</th><td>{{ change.unit }}</td><td class="num">{{ source_mark(change.expert_ref, change.expert) }}</td><td class="num">{{ source_mark(change.mine_ref, change.mine) }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </article>
  {% endfor %}
</section>
{% endblock %}
